/*
  core/masks/share_behavior.spthy -- f_H for the SHARE action class, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC (AGNOSTIC_MASKS.md).
  The ceremony reports only OBSERVABLES in !StepData(P, rid, <recipient, correspondent, secret>):
  who this share would go to (the reply-to / entered address), who the ceremony is actually WITH
  (the known correspondent), and the payload. The VERDICT is derived HERE, like compare/confirm
  (repo MEMORY.md lesson 14): the Attentive rule PERFORMS the recipient check -- matches
  recipient = correspondent (you disclose the secret only to the person the ceremony is with) --
  so a phishing reply-prompt whose reply-to is NOT the correspondent stalls an Attentive user.
  The degraded masks do not look. This is what lets phishing EMERGE from an open mail channel
  instead of being a hard-coded lure: a spoofed display name still delivers to the REAL
  correspondent (harmless); capturing the secret requires a degraded recipient.

    Attentive ('oob')          : recipient = correspondent -> secret off the wire.        -> Oob only
    Careless ('inband-leak')   : in-band leak; intended recipient still gets it (silent). -> Out+Oob
    Busy     ('misdeliver')    : fat-fingered to the wrong place; intended one locked out. -> Out

  The BEHAVIOUR (mask -> outcome + the Share/LeakPw/MisdeliveredPw actions) lives here; a thin
  per-ceremony EFFECT ADAPTER (secure_email interface/effects.spthy) turns the generic
  ShareOutcome(P,rid,kind) + the !StepData observables into the channel facts (Out / Oob).
  RespMask(P,mask) gated by mask_state.spthy as before.
*/

// Attentive: performs the recipient check -- shares only with the actual correspondent.
rule Share_oob [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !StepData(P, rid, <r, r, pw>), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'oob') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), ShareOOB(P, rid) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'oob') ]

rule Share_inband_leak [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'inband-leak') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), LeakPw(P), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'inband-leak') ]

rule Share_misdeliver [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'misdeliver') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), MisdeliveredPw(P), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'misdeliver') ]
